  "result": {
    "answer": "## 回答\nViT 在 ImageNet-21k 数据集和 JFT-300M 数据集上进行了预训练。[参考文档1：Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第2页（物理页码）][参考文档2：Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第4页（物理页码）]\n\n具体来说，使用了 ImageNet-21k 数据集，该数据集包含 21,000 个类别和 14,000,000 张图像。[参考文档2：Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第4页（物理页码）] 同时，还使用了 JFT 数据集，该数据集包含 18,000 个类别。[参考文档3：Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第6页（物理页码）]\n\n## 参考来源\n- [参考文档1] Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第2页（物理页码）\n- [参考文档2] Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第4页（物理页码）\n- [参考文档3] Windows验收\\_ViT.pdf；第6页（物理页码）",
    "citations": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "source_file": "Windows验收_ViT.pdf",
        "location": "第2页（物理页码）",
        "text": "\npre-trained on the public ImageNet-21k dataset or the in-house JFT-300M dataset, ViT approaches\nor beats state of the art on multiple image recognition benchmarks. In particular, the best model\nreaches the accuracy of 88.55% on ImageNet, 90.72% on ImageNet-ReaL, 94.55% on CIFAR-100,\nand 77.63% on the VTAB suite of 19 tasks.\n2\nRELATED WORK\nTransformers were proposed by Vaswani et al. (2017) for machine translation, and have since be-",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk_id": "9b043bf909596310b3e93dd842ed1b2f1e77ab141d8616dee3c9f177be0dcea4",
          "doc_id": "8ce7b83971a14508ca711a27c875c9b6914c4f6767cf3150fb1ca6c07aa056d6",
          "file_type": ".pdf",
          "page": 1,
          "page_number": 2,
          "source": "E:\\工作\\RAG-Agent\\.test-tmp\\win-simplify-20261009\\probe\\raw\\8ce7b83971a14508ca711a27c875c9b6914c4f6767cf3150fb1ca6c07aa056d6\\Windows验收_ViT.pdf",
          "source_file": "Windows验收_ViT.pdf"
        },
        "truncated": false,
        "score": 0.9988046884536743
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "source_file": "Windows验收_ViT.pdf",
        "location": "第4页（物理页码）",
        "text": "\na lower pre-training cost. Lastly, we perform a small experiment using self-supervision, and show\nthat self-supervised ViT holds promise for the future.\n4.1\nSETUP\nDatasets. To explore model scalability, we use the ILSVRC-2012 ImageNet dataset with 1k classes\nand 1.3M images (we refer to it as ImageNet in what follows), its superset ImageNet-21k with\n21k classes and 14M images (Deng et al., 2009), and JFT (Sun et al., 2017) with 18k classes and",
        "metadata": {
          "chunk_id": "abe2f1d08bd659d3bfb96dc5918c09824c6db2b3b3ef1255557393dabfe91510",
          "doc_id": "8ce7b83971a14508ca711a27c875c9b6914c4f6767cf3150fb1ca6c07aa056d6",
          "file_type": ".pdf",
          "page": 3,
          "page_number": 4,
          "source": "E:\\工作\\RAG-Agent\\.test-tmp\\win-simplify-20261009\\probe\\raw\\8ce7b83971a14508ca711a27c875c9b6914c4f6767cf3150fb1ca6c07aa056d6\\Windows验收_ViT.pdf",
          "source_file": "Windows验收_ViT.pdf"
        },
        "truncated": false,
        "score": 0.9963682889938354
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "source_file": "Windows验收_ViT.pdf",
        "location": "第6页（物理页码）",
        "text": "\ntuning to ImageNet (results on other datasets are shown in Table 5)^{2}. When pre-trained on the\nsmallest dataset, ImageNet, ViT-Large models underperform compared to ViT-Base models, despite\n(moderate) regularization. With ImageNet-21k pre-training, their performances are similar. Only\nwith JFT-300M, do we see the full beneﬁt of larger models. Figure 3 also shows the performance\n^{2}Note that the ImageNet pre-trained models are also ﬁne-tuned, but again on ImageNet. This is because the",
